    <string name="settings_about">About</string>
    <string name="settings_about_summary">Who made this app, and why</string>
    <string name="about_story">I\'m a hobbyist developer, and to be honest this app was put together with the help of Claude Code, because time is the thing I have least of.\n\nIt started as something for myself: I wanted to stop digging through web apps in the middle of a game and just be comfortable while playing.</string>
    <string name="about_note_title">One important note</string>
    <string name="about_note">The app grows in step with my own collection. I would rather add a campaign after playing it myself, so that I know the rules well enough to give players a good experience, than add one I have no experience with.\n\nFeel free to get in touch — I am glad to hear from you.</string>
    <string name="about_contact">Contact me</string>
    <string name="about_version">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_disclaimer">An unofficial fan-made app, free and not for sale. Not produced by, endorsed by, or affiliated with Marvel, Fantasy Flight Games or Asmodee. Marvel Champions: The Card Game and all related names and artwork belong to their respective owners. You need the physical game to play; this app does not replace the rules or the cards.</string>
    <string name="about_data_source">Card data comes from MarvelCDB, whose contributors maintain it. Thank you to them.</string>
    <string name="about_no_ads">This app carries no advertising, and it never will. I turn down every advertising offer and sponsorship proposal I receive for it. It is free, it collects nothing about you, and it exists so that a game night runs a little more smoothly.</string>
